# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

Accessibility failures are bugs that block real people. Follow these phases when auditing,
and the "Fix" rules whenever you write UI.

## 1. Static scan
Run `npx @mintwork/wcag-audit-skill scan <path> --json --fail-on none` in the terminal. Group findings
by component — many call-site findings usually share one root-cause component. Also review
manually: shared primitives (Button/IconButton/Input/Modal) forward aria-* and id; no
`outline: none` / `focus:outline-none` without a `:focus-visible` replacement; state is not
conveyed by color alone; errors are tied to fields with `aria-describedby`.

## 2. Runtime scan
If a dev server is running, run `npx @mintwork/wcag-audit-skill scan http://localhost:<port>/<page> --json --fail-on none`.
It uses axe-core in a real browser plus Tab-key checks for keyboard traps and invisible focus.
Add `--source src` for source hints, `--config <file>` for states (open modal, dark mode, 320px),
`--storage-state <file>` for logged-in pages and `--storybook <url|dir>` to scan every story.

## 3. Verify every finding
Open the reported file:line. Try to disprove it: trace props, spreads, slots and parents.
Confirmed → fix. Unclear (alt text meaning, unreachable state) → ask the user. Disproved → drop.

## 4. Fix (always, also when writing new UI)
- Mechanical findings (`html-lang`, `meta-viewport-zoom`, `aria-*` typos): `scan <path> --dry-run`, show the diff, then `--fix`.
- Native elements first: `<button type="button">` for actions, `<a href>` for navigation. Never `<div onClick>`.
- Every input has a `<label htmlFor>` (or wrapping `<label>`); placeholder is not a label.
- Images: meaningful `alt`; `alt=""` only if decorative. Never `alt="image"`. Don't invent content — ask.
- Icon-only buttons/links: `aria-label="<action>"`, icon gets `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Headings descend one level at a time; change the level, keep the CSS.
- No positive `tabindex`. Visible `:focus-visible` style on every interactive element.
- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (3:1 for large text). Ask before changing brand colors.
- `<html lang>`, a descriptive `<title>`, and never disable zoom in the viewport meta.
- Modals: focus moves in on open, Escape closes, focus returns to the trigger; prefer `<dialog>`.
Explain each fix in one sentence: what was wrong, who it affected, what changed.

## 5. Re-check and report
Save the scan with `--json -o /tmp/a11y.json`, then `npx @mintwork/wcag-audit-skill verify /tmp/a11y.json`
after fixing (non-zero exit = remaining or new issues). Report counts by severity, fixes, open
questions, and what automation can't check (screen reader pass, zoom/reflow, captions).
